    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.118 UBTU-24-700060"
      info        : "The operating system must configure the directories used by the system journal to be group-owned by \"systemd-journal\".

GROUP ID: V-270761
RULE ID: SV-270761r1067180

Only authorized personnel should be aware of errors and the details of the errors. Error messages are an indicator of an organization's operational state or can identify the operating system or platform. Additionally, personally identifiable information (PII) and operational information must not be revealed through error messages to unauthorized personnel or their designated representatives.

The structure and content of error messages must be carefully considered by the organization and development team. The extent to which the information system is able to identify and handle error conditions is guided by organizational policy and operational requirements."
      solution    : "Configure the operating system to set the appropriate group-ownership to the directories used by the systemd journal:

Add or modify the following lines in the \"/usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/systemd.conf\" file:

z /run/log/journal 2640 root systemd-journal - -
z /var/log/journal 2640 root systemd-journal - -

Restart the system for the changes to take effect."
      reference   : "800-53|SI-11b.,800-53r5|SI-11b.,800-53r5|SI-11c.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001314,CSCv7|14.6,CSCv8|3.3,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SI-11c.,LEVEL|2A,Rule-ID|SV-270761r1067180_rule,STIG-ID|UBTU-24-700060,Vuln-ID|V-270761"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22775"
      cmd         : "/bin/find /run/log/journal /var/log/journal ! -group systemd-journal -type d -exec stat -c \"%n %G\" '{}' \\; | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"All directories are owned by group systemd-journal\"}'"
      expect      : "^All directories are owned by group systemd-journal$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
