    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.184 UBTU-24-901300"
      info        : "The operating system must be configured so that audit log files are not read- or write-accessible by unauthorized users.

GROUP ID: V-270827
RULE ID: SV-270827r1066970

Unauthorized disclosure of audit records can reveal system and configuration data to attackers, thus compromising its confidentiality.

Audit information includes all information (e.g., audit records, audit settings, audit reports) needed to successfully audit operating system activity.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027, SRG-OS-000058-GPOS-00028"
      solution    : "Configure the audit log files to have a mode of \"600\" or less permissive.

Using the path of the directory containing the audit logs, configure the audit log files to have a mode of \"600\" or less permissive by using the following command:

$ sudo chmod 600 /var/log/audit/*"
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.8,800-171r3|03.03.08,800-53|AU-9,800-53r5|AU-9a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000162,CCI|CCI-000163,CN-L3|7.1.2.3(d),CN-L3|7.1.3.3(f),CN-L3|8.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.3(c),CSCv7|14.6,CSCv8|3.3,CSF|PR.PT-1,CSF2.0|PR.DS-10,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.33,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.15,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.4.2,ITSG-33|AU-9,LEVEL|2A,NESA|M5.2.3,NESA|M5.5.2,NESA|T3.6.4,NESA|T8.2.9,NIAv2|SM5,NIAv2|SM6,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.5,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.5.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|10.3.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-270827r1066970_rule,STIG-ID|UBTU-24-901300,Vuln-ID|V-270827"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22775"
      cmd         : "logfile=$(/bin/grep -iw ^\\s*log_file /etc/audit/auditd.conf); if [ ! -z \"${logfile}\" ]; then /bin/stat -c \"%n %a\" $(/bin/dirname ${logfile} | /bin/grep \"/\")/* | /bin/grep -Ev '0?[0-6]00' | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"All files have a mode of 0600 or less\"; else print \"Failing files found\"}'; else echo \"log_file variable in /etc/audit/auditd.conf not set\"; fi"
      expect      : "^All files have a mode of 0600 or less$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.185 UBTU-24-901310"
      info        : "The operating system must be configured to permit only authorized users ownership of the audit log files.

GROUP ID: V-270828
RULE ID: SV-270828r1066973

Unauthorized disclosure of audit records can reveal system and configuration data to attackers, thus compromising its confidentiality.

Audit information includes all information (e.g., audit records, audit settings, audit reports) needed to successfully audit operating system activity.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027, SRG-OS-000058-GPOS-00028, SRG-OS-000059-GPOS-00029"
