    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.61 UBTU-24-300014"
      info        : "The operating system must prevent the use of dictionary words for passwords.

GROUP ID: V-270704
RULE ID: SV-270704r1066601

If the operating system allows the user to select passwords based on dictionary words, then this increases the chances of password compromise by increasing the opportunity for successful guesses and brute-force attacks."
      solution    : "Configure the operating system to prevent the use of dictionary words for passwords.

Add or modify the following line in the \"/etc/security/pwquality.conf\" file:

dictcheck = 1"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSCv7|4.4,CSCv8|5.2,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-270704r1066601_rule,STIG-ID|UBTU-24-300014,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-270704"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22775"
      file        : "/etc/security/pwquality.conf"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*dictcheck"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*dictcheck[\\s]*=[\\s]*@PASSWORD_DICTCHECK@[\\s]*$"
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
